  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "03_Authorization-in-ASP.NET Core",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Goal",
      "description": "How to Enfore practice control in our backend using Authorization features of .Net Core\n\n\n- The need for authorization\n- Require authorization in ASP.NET Core\n- Role-based authorization\n- Claims-based authorization\n- Policy-based authorization\n- Authorization by default\n- Anonymous access\n- Resource-based authorization\n"
    },
    {
      "title": "Section 00",
      "description": "# Authentication and Authorization :\n\n## Authentication : \"Who are you?\"\n\nDefinition: The process of verifying the identity of a user or system.\n\nPurpose: Proves you are who you claim to be before granting access.\n\n### How it works:\n\nUser provides credentials (username/password, token, certificate, biometrics) \n\nSystem validates these credentials against a trusted source\nUpon success, system creates an identity (typically a ClaimsPrincipal in ASP.NET Core)\n\nUser receives an access token (commonly JWT) for subsequent requests\n\n## Authorization: \"What can you do?\"\n\nDefinition: Determining what an authenticated user is allowed to do.\n\nPurpose: Enforces access control policies after identity is verified.\n\n# Types of Authorization in ASP.NET Core \n\n1. Role-Based Authorization\n    - Definition: Checks if an authenticated user belongs to a specific role (e.g., Admin, User, Manager).\n2. Claims-Based Authorization\n    - Definition: Uses specific user or client attributes (claims) to make authorization decisions. Claims are key-value pairs describing the user.\n3. Policy-Based Authorization\n    - Definition: Combines multiple requirements (roles, claims, custom logic) into reusable named policies.\n\n    When to use: Complex authorization scenarios or when you need to reuse the same set of requirements across multiple endpoints.\n\n4. Resource-Based Authorization\n    - Definition: Authorization decisions are based on the specific resource being accessed. Requires checking the resource's properties at runtime.\n\n    When to use:\n\n    Users can only edit their own data Access depends on resource ownership Dynamic permissions based on resource state"
    },
    {
      "title": "Section 01",
