    {
      "title": "Section 04",
      "description": "Using policy-based authorization"
    },
    {
      "file": "Notes/02_Authorization-in-ASP.NET Core/Lesson04.06/src/GameStore.Api/Shared/Authorization/Policies.cs",
      "description": "Purpose: Centralizes policy names for authorization, avoiding hard-coded strings across the app.",
      "line": 3
    },
    {
      "file": "Notes/02_Authorization-in-ASP.NET Core/Lesson04.06/src/GameStore.Api/Program.cs",
      "description": "add this : \n                \n```csharp\n                .AddPolicy(Policies.UserAccess, authBuilder =>\n                {\n                    authBuilder.RequireClaim(\"scope\", \"gamestore_api.all\");\n                })\n                .AddPolicy(Policies.AdminAccess, authBuilder =>\n                {\n                    authBuilder.RequireClaim(\"scope\", \"gamestore_api.all\");\n                    authBuilder.RequireRole(Roles.Admin);\n                });   \n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n### Behavior\n\n- Missing/invalid token: 401 Unauthorized (authentication fails).\n- Valid token without required claim/role: 403 Forbidden (authenticated but not authorized).\n- Valid token with required claim/role: Request proceeds.\n\n### Usage\n\n- Protect endpoints with named policies:\n- .RequireAuthorization(Policies.UserAccess) for general API-read access.\n- .RequireAuthorization(Policies.AdminAccess) for admin-only operations.\n",
      "line": 41
    },
